{"items": [{"id": "H1", "scope": "annotation", "category": "taxonomy", "title": "Use a colon marker list, not the small-intestine list", "text": "This sigmoid colon was annotated with the small-intestine list, which lacks colonocytes and real colonic goblet cells. As a result, 9,064 cells (22%) are called Cycling TAs, but only one sub-cluster (1,121 cells) expresses MKI67/TOP2A; sub-cluster /8 (1,410) is SLC26A3+/CA1+ colonocytes, and 3,353 'BEST4+ enterocytes' have BEST4 in only 10% but CEACAM7, AQP8 and GUCA2A (mature colonocytes); only 79 goblet cells were found. Draft a colon list (organ_marker_draft colon) with Colonocytes and goblet markers, without Enterocytes, Paneth cells (your prior U-1) and M cells, and re-annotate.", "action": {"kind": "claude", "request": "Draft a marker list for sample 167799 from organ_marker_draft(organ='colon'), keeping the stromal/immune refinements of the current list, check it and propose it."}, "status": "open", "version": 1, "time": "2026-11-13T12:38:03", "check": {"keep": true, "reason": "Confirmed: the SI list forces colonic epithelium into SI types.", "evidence": "type_structure: only Cycling TAs /4 (1,121 of 9,064) is MKI67/TOP2A+ (76\u201380%); /8 (1,410) is SLC26A3 90%/CA1 97% colonocytes. BEST4+ enterocytes (3,353): BEST4 10%, sub-clusters are GPX2/CFTR, SELENBP1/CD24, CYP3A4 colonocytes and a REP15/HEPACAM2 goblet-like group; Goblet cells only 79. Enterocytes\u2013BEST4 confusion 0.28.", "time": "2026-11-13T12:38:18"}}, {"id": "H2", "scope": "annotation", "category": "taxonomy", "title": "Venules merged into Capillary EC", "text": "All 3,643 blood vessel EC became Capillary EC, yet ACKR1 (venule marker) is detected in 42% of them and CA4 in only 5%; Venous EC was not found. Split blood vessel EC by ACKR1 (venules) and relax the capillary markers (drop CA4 as required).", "action": {"kind": "claude", "request": "Edit the endothelial part of the list: Venous EC ACKR1+ PLVAP+, Capillary EC CD36+ NOTCH4+ ACKR1-, and re-annotate."}, "status": "open", "version": 1, "time": "2026-11-13T12:38:03", "check": {"keep": true, "reason": "Confirmed and broader: 'Capillary EC' holds venules and arterial EC too.", "evidence": "type_structure Capillary EC: /2 + /3 (1,657 cells) ACKR1 73\u201392%, MMRN1/CPE (venules); /1 (843) HEY1 76%, RERGL (arterial); only /0 (819) CD36/RGS5 capillary. CA4 5% overall.", "time": "2026-11-13T12:38:18"}}, {"id": "H3", "scope": "annotation", "category": "taxonomy", "title": "gd T cells called NK cells", "text": "TRDC is detected in 70% of the 20 'NK cells' and gd T cells were not found; these are likely gd intraepithelial T cells (COL-09).", "action": null, "status": "filtered", "version": 1, "time": "2026-11-13T12:38:03", "check": {"keep": false, "reason": "Only 20 cells; a real but negligible mislabel, not worth a change on its own (fold into the next list edit).", "evidence": "", "time": "2026-11-13T12:38:18"}}, {"id": "H4", "scope": "annotation", "category": "context", "title": "Draw the mucosa so the colon priors apply", "text": "No regions are drawn, so COL-01 (epithelium only in the mucosa) and your U-1 (no Paneth cells) cannot act. The epithelium outlines the mucosa well (4 pieces, 98.6% of epithelial cells inside, matching the crypt layer on the H&E). Draw it and add COL-01.", "action": {"kind": "region", "name": "mucosa", "compartment": "mucosa", "n_cells": 19907, "prior": {"text": "COL-01: epithelial cells lie in the mucosa", "kind": "region", "types": ["Epithelial"], "regions": ["mucosa"], "mode": "only", "weight": "strong"}, "prior_text": "COL-01: epithelial cells lie in the mucosa (only found in [mucosa]; elsewhere prior x0.01)", "outlines": [[[5577.36756159724, 791.6610489304296], [5711.974687382002, 797.2031377110147], [5784.2503587406445, 843.1684656103034], [5856.526030099287, 855.3001166247575], [5899.891432914472, 874.9665186554314], [5908.555280453334, 892.8469888325287], [5924.269568891974, 1022.9431972780851], [5915.772585872191, 1138.584271451